0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-up-right ml-auto size-3.5 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground/30 transition-[rotate,color] duration-500 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.22,1,0.36,1)] group-hover:rotate-45 group-hover:text-foreground\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10\"></path><path d=\"M7 17 17 7\"></path></svg></div></div></a></div><section class=\"mx-auto mt-16 max-w-2xl\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-heading\"><h2 id=\"faq-heading\" class=\"text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]\">FAQ</h2><dl class=\"mt-4 space-y-5\"><div><dt class=\"text-[0.95rem] font-medium\">Do the charts need a charting library?</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">No. They are drawn by hand in SVG and canvas with the dither and shader fills, take plain arrays as data, and come with hover detail, keyboard access and a screen-reader description of the data.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"text-[0.95rem] font-medium\">How do I install the components in Charts?</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">With the shadcn CLI. Each component page lists its exact command: free components install from a public URL (npx shadcn add https://useplanes.com/r/&lt;name&gt;.json), Pro components install by name (npx shadcn add @useplanes/&lt;name&gt;) after npx @useplanes/cli init --key &lt;key&gt;.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"text-[0.95rem] font-medium\">Do they work with Next.js App Router and Tailwind CSS v4?</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Yes. Every component is a React 19 client component styled with Tailwind CSS v4, and works in Next.js App Router, Vite, or any React app with Tailwind CSS v4.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"text-[0.95rem] font-medium\">Are the components in Charts free?</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">They are part of Planes Pro, a one-time license that covers every component and future additions. The catalog also has free components in other categories.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"text-[0.95rem] font-medium\">What do they depend on?</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Motion (formerly Framer Motion) is the only runtime animation dependency. The CLI writes the .tsx source into your project, so there is no Planes package to keep updated.</dd></div></dl></section></section>"}